+# Legacy i386 port notes
+
+## Upstream base
+
+- Project: GNU C Library
+- Release: 2.43
+- Source: `https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/glibc/glibc-2.43.tar.xz`
+- SHA-256:
+  `d9c86c6b5dbddb43a3e08270c5844fc5177d19442cf5b8df4be7c07cd5fa3831`
+- Local upstream snapshot tag: `upstream-2.43`
+
+The `upstream` branch records pristine stable-release snapshots. Legacy
+i386 changes belong on `main` as separate reviewable commits.
+
+## Current status
+
+This repository is the source baseline for a future genuine i386 glibc
+port. No PC-98 or legacy-i386 source changes have been applied yet, and the
+current tree is not claimed to run on an Intel 80386.
+
+The first implementation phase must identify the current minimum CPU
+assumptions, atomic operations, TLS and pthread requirements, compiler
+runtime dependencies, and generated multiarch code before changing the
+public ABI.
+
+PC-98-specific device or firmware behavior must stay in the kernel and
+loader. Changes here should be useful to other legacy i386 Linux systems,
+including future FM TOWNS ports.
